Recommends: composefs
Static-Built-Using: ${misc:Static-Built-Using}
Description: OCI-native content delivery and mount engine for edge devices
 ocicfs pulls standard OCI images into a shared content-addressed store and
 mounts them with composefs, EROFS and fs-verity: one mount syscall per
 image, a single decompressed copy of content on disk, and no daemon.
 .
 The mount, unmount, ls, inspect, hold, release, remove and gc commands
 work out of the box. pull and seal build EROFS images via mkcomposefs and
 need the composefs package (or another source of mkcomposefs) installed.
